ANN = Artificial Neural Network (basic neural network)

DNN = Deep Neural Network (ANN with multiple hidden layers)

CNN = Convolutional Neural Network (specialized DNN for image processing)

One-Line Answer

DNN is a deep version of ANN containing multiple hidden layers, whereas CNN is a specialized DNN used for image and video processing. 

===========

ANN vs DNN vs CNN

| Feature            | ANN                                     | DNN                                 | CNN                                            |
| ------------------ | --------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| Full Form          | Artificial Neural Network               | Deep Neural Network                 | Convolutional Neural Network                   |
| Structure          | Input + 1 or Few Hidden Layers + Output | Input + Many Hidden Layers + Output | Convolution + Pooling + Fully Connected Layers |
| Data Type          | Structured Data                         | Large Complex Data                  | Images & Videos                                |
| Feature Extraction | Manual                                  | Learns Features                     | Automatically Learns Image Features            |
| Accuracy           | Lower                                   | Higher                              | Very High for Images                           |
| Training Time      | Fast                                    | Moderate                            | High                                           |
| Image Processing   | Not Suitable                            | Limited                             | Excellent                                      |
| Examples           | Salary Prediction                       | Speech Recognition                  | Face Detection                                 |

